0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"What truly sets us apart is our commitment to staying at the frontier of AI advancements. We relentlessly innovate, introducing new features and improvements at a pace unmatched in the industry. And we ensure that every leap we take forward integrates your valuable feedback because at Leonardo.Ai, creators are the drivers of our mission."})]})},{question:"How do models work?",answer:(0,t.jsxs)("div",{className:"text-secondary-foreground space-y-4",children:[(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"At Leonardo.Ai, we believe in versatility. Our platform isn't restricted to a single generalised model; instead, we have an assortment of both general and finely-tuned models, each crafted to excel in various types of content generation. This variety lets users go beyond a one-size-fits-all approach and select the model that best suits their specific image type or use case."}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"To provide even greater customisation, we offer the option for users to train/fine-tune their own models. Users can upload a small collection of images (typically 10-20) to train a unique model that recreates a specific style, theme, or subject. This fine-tuning process can pick up nuanced aspects, like color patterns, composition, and even aesthetic concepts, resulting in style-consistent image generation."}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"Remember, these models aren't restricted to any specific field. From art and design to gaming and beyond, our models can cater to just about any creative pursuit."})]})},{question:"Will I own the images I make?",answer:(0,t.jsxs)("div",{className:"text-secondary-foreground space-y-4",children:[(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"Your image ownership rights differ based on your Leonardo.Ai subscription status:"}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:[(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Paid subscribers:"})," Yes, you retain full ownership, copyright, and other intellectual property rights of images that you generate. Leonardo.Ai may use your private images only to provide you with our services. Public images can be used by Leonardo.Ai and other users, only as enabled by a feature of the service."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:[(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Free tier users:"}),"Leonardo.Ai holds rights to use, reproduce, modify, and distribute any images you create. However, you're granted a non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to access your creations for commercial use. Other users can also access your publicly available assets and use them only as enabled by a feature of the service."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["For more detailed information, please refer to our"," ",(0,t.jsx)("a",{target:"_blank",href:"https://leonardo.ai/terms-of-service/",rel:"noreferrer",className:"text-highlight-foreground hover:underline",children:"Terms of Service"}),"."]})]})},{question:"Tokens and Token Rollover at Leonardo.Ai",answer:(0,t.jsxs)("div",{className:"text-secondary-foreground space-y-4",children:[(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"Tokens are effectively your 'currency' on the Leonardo.Ai platform, deducted from your account balance as you perform various actions—including generating images, creating videos, post-processing tasks like background removal, and upscale conversions."}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"The number of tokens used is based on the computational intensity of the action you're taking—the more GPU load required, the more tokens are charged. One key thing to note: a single token doesn't correspond to a specific image size or a specific action. The token cost adjusts based on the complexity and computational requirements of the task you're performing."}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"If you're a free user, you're allocated a certain number of tokens each day, and these reset for you daily, allowing you to perform actions within this limit."}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"As a paid subscriber, you receive a monthly token allowance that gives you much wider flexibility to use Leonardo.Ai's premium features at your own pace. Importantly, these tokens reset and replenish at the beginning of each billing month, so you always start with a fresh balance."}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"Additionally, Leonardo.Ai offers on premium plans a Token Rollover feature, allowing you to retain unused tokens from the previous cycle. These leftover tokens are transferred to a Rollover Bank, with limits based on your plan type. This ensures you can maximize the value of your premium plan by carrying over unused tokens instead of losing them. You can check your Rollover Bank by hovering over the token counter on the app's main page."}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"Paid users can also purchase Token Top-up packs, which never expire and are not affected by rollover limits. These tokens are only usable while subscribed."})]})},{question:"What happens if I run out of tokens in my paid plan?",answer:(0,t.jsx)("div",{className:"text-secondary-foreground",children:(0,t.jsxs)("ul",{className:"list-disc pl-5",children:[(0,t.jsx)("li",{children:"Subscribed users can buy Token Top-up packs to continue creating."}),(0,t.jsx)("li",{children:"Top-up Tokens do not expire and are used after Rollover Tokens and Fast Tokens."}),(0,t.jsx)("li",{children:"Top-up Tokens require an active subscription to be used."})]})})},{question:"What is Token Rollover and How Does it Work?",answer:(0,t.jsxs)("div",{className:"text-secondary-foreground space-y-4",children:[(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"Token Rollover allows users to retain unused tokens from the previous cycle when their tokens reset. This ensures users can maximize the value of their premium plans by carrying over unused tokens instead of losing them."}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"Leonardo.Ai transfers leftover tokens to a Rollover Bank, with the maximum limit based on the user's plan type. Users can check their Rollover Bank by hovering over the token counter on the app's main page."})]})},{question:'How do the "Unlimited" Plans and "Relaxed Generation" work?',answer:(0,t.jsxs)("div",{className:"text-secondary-foreground",children:[(0,t.jsx)("h4",{className:"text-base font-semibold",children:"Who gets it?"}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Subscribers on our ",(0,t.jsx)("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:n.PLAN_TO_NAME.STANDARD})," and"," ",(0,t.jsx)("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:n.PLAN_TO_NAME.PRO}),"plans receive a large pool of tokens each billing cycle. When that pool hits zero, you don't lose access to new generations—instead you create new images or videos using our"," ",(0,t.jsx)("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:"Relaxed Generation"})," feature."]}),(0,t.jsx)("h4",{className:"mt-4 text-base font-semibold",children:"What is it?"}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"Relaxed Generation lets you keep generating images and videos without extra token cost, but at a lower priority than the main queue. Processing time fluctuates with overall demand: if the priority queue is busy, your job waits a little longer; if it's quiet, it finishes faster. To prevent longer waiting times, the number of concurrent generations are also reduced. You can still create as much as you want, it may just take a little longer so we can ensure fair and equitable access and stability for other users."}),(0,t.jsx)("h4",{className:"mt-4 text-base font-semibold",children:"Which models are eligible?"}),(0,t.jsxs)("ul",{className:"list-disc pl-5",children:[(0,t.jsx)("li",{children:"Eligible first-party models: Lucid Origin, Lucid Realism, Phoenix 1.0, Phoenix 0.9, FLUX Dev, FLUX Schnell, Motion 2.0, Motion 2.0 Fast. These can be used with Relaxed Generation."}),(0,t.jsxs)("li",{children:["Third-party models; ",(0,t.jsx)("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:"GPT-Image-1"}),", ",(0,t.jsx)("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:"GPT Image 1.5"}),","," ",(0,t.jsx)("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:"GPT Image 2"}),", ",(0,t.jsx)("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:"Flux.1 Kontext"}),","," ",(0,t.jsx)("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:"Ideogram"}),", ",(0